			<div class="content" id="post-content-4828752">
									

<p>So glad to see this here, it's super fun!</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Of&nbsp;course,&nbsp;I'll&nbsp;always&nbsp;have&nbsp;nitpicks</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">But&nbsp;the&nbsp;overall&nbsp;here&nbsp;is&nbsp;great!</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<blockquote>
<p>&#8230;and the ability to increase and decrease height in levitation.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Strange phrasing here. Maybe you wanted &quot;&#8230;and the ability to increase and decrease the height at which it's levitating.&quot;</p>
<hr />
<blockquote>
<p>It is capable of firing non-anomalous revolver ammunition, however, its anomalous properties include a seemingly limitless supply of ammunition and the ability to fire explosive or non-explosive rounds.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Long, unwieldy sentence when combined. I think the problem might be the transition between the ideas, Maybe it'd be better as &quot;&#8230;capable of firing non-anomalous revolver ammunition, but its anomalous&#8230;&quot;</p>
<hr />
<blockquote>
<p>NOTE: Employee Glenn Briggs is feeding the horses when he encounters SCP-4576.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Veeery minor, but because we haven't been introduced to this horse yet, it's not <em>the</em> horse to us, it's just <em>a</em> horse.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>But yeah, super fun. That last addendum is messed up, but the good kind of messed up.</p>

